we continue isolating $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & <x+5\\le 6 \\\\ 3-5 & <x+5-5\\le 6-5 \\\\ -2 & <x\\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $-2<x\\le 1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069228 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068686 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5930113e-6971-59c9-810a-97fd25bc4f89" :knowledge-point/title "Compound Inequalities That Require Flipping the Inequality Sign"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc51915d-9f31-5d2b-8475-af5750338981" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15 < x < 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066547} {:answer/id #uuid "d1a8075d-79db-5b7f-93ed-6c8f3546511e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 < x < 15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066548} {:answer/id #uuid "ddbc07f0-1a83-5eb5-9ee9-ec2b1a3783cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 < x < 16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066549} {:answer/id #uuid "2ab6de6b-f8b3-567e-990f-a054408be3a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18 < x < 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066550} {:answer/id #uuid "7b367a60-d8d4-5ca7-9ad4-68197390e74f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 < x < 18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066551}] :answer-field/id #uuid "5696f866-cced-54cd-962d-9825c54cd08a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066546}] :question/id #uuid "b61c5dfe-34c0-5830-8c59-cd20d813f4bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-3070" :question/problem "What is the solution to $-10 < \\frac{6 - 2x}{3} < 0$?"}]}
